"Expands sequential choices and uncertain events into mutually distinguishable paths leading to decision consequences.\n\nUse when: Compare options when later uncertainty changes their value. Explain which observations arrive before a subsequent choice.\n\nAvoid when: A compact dependency overview or simultaneous strategic interaction is sufficient.\n\nVisual grammar: Decision nodes denote controllable alternatives; chance nodes denote uncertain outcomes. Labeled branches express choices or conditional events. Terminal leaves show consequences in consistent units.\n\nBuild: State the decision owner, objective and time horizon. Expand choices and chance events in their actual information order. Attach justified probabilities or qualitative uncertainty and evaluate complete paths.\n\nCheck: Chance probabilities sum to one within each modeled condition. Choices use information available at that point. All relevant consequence dimensions and path costs are included.\n\nPitfalls: Treating a competitor's purposeful response as a fixed random draw. Comparing monetary and nonmonetary leaf values as if interchangeable.\n\nExample: A retailer chooses whether to run a pilot, observes demand and then decides whether to launch a new service.\n\nAlternatives: Influence diagram, Game tree."
